From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caleb Ethridge <caleb.ethridge@analog.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:56:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] testptp: Print the clock time correctly with a 64-bit time_t

On 32-bit targets built with a 64-bit time_t, such as ARMv7 with
_TIME_BITS=64, printing tv_sec with %ld misaligns the printf
arguments, so "testptp -g" printed garbage and could crash in ctime().
Print tv_sec as a long long, as the other times in testptp are.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Caleb Ethridge <caleb.ethridge@analog.com>
---
 testptp.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/testptp.c b/testptp.c
index 08daebb..bea2553 100644
--- a/testptp.c
+++ b/testptp.c
@@ -316,8 +316,8 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 		if (clock_gettime(clkid, &ts)) {
 			perror("clock_gettime");
 		} else {
-			printf("clock time: %ld.%09ld or %s",
-			       ts.tv_sec, ts.tv_nsec, ctime(&ts.tv_sec));
+			printf("clock time: %lld.%09ld or %s",
+			       (long long)ts.tv_sec, ts.tv_nsec, ctime(&ts.tv_sec));
 		}
 	}
 
